      "content": "A \"minor regulatory hurdle\" might be a stretch if they see the actual filings. If I tell them it's just standard administrative stuff, am I basically lying to them? I don't want to get sued for fraud later if the patent actually gets invalidated in a few months. Is there a way to stay \"truthful\" without actually giving them the bad news and losing our valuation?",
